Lab 6: Testing Camel Routes with JUnit
Objectives
By the end of this lab, students will be able to:

Set up unit tests for Apache Camel routes using the JUnit 5 framework
Create and configure mock endpoints to simulate external systems
Write test cases that validate route behavior with different inputs
Use Camel test assertions to verify message processing and routing logic
Interpret Maven Surefire test output to confirm route correctness
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, students should have:

Basic understanding of Apache Camel concepts (routes, endpoints, processors)
Familiarity with Java programming language
Knowledge of Maven build tool and dependency management
Understanding of unit testing concepts and experience with JUnit
Completed previous Camel labs covering basic route creation
Lab Environment: This lab is performed on a self-owned or sandboxed practice machine (a local workstation or an assigned cloud lab machine). All work is local â�� no external network calls or third-party systems are involved, which makes this a safe, fully isolated environment for learning integration testing techniques.

